       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily for adults. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia, and they usually add little extra blood pressure control.\n\nHere are some options:\n1. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Enter 10 mg now and add a second agent**, such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide, if 10 mg isn't enough. This is usually more effective than raising amlodipine further.\n3. **Enter 20 mg as written**, if you want that dose for a specific clinical reason. Tell me, and I'll enter it with a note documenting that it's an intentional above-maximum dose.\n\nWhich would you like?"
      }
